# Line endings are the repository's business, not each machine's.
#
# This worked by accident until now: `core.autocrlf=true` happens to be set on
# the development machine, so history holds LF and the working tree holds CRLF.
# That setting is local config — it does not travel with a clone. The first
# checkout on a machine without it commits CRLF blobs, the stored form of the
# file flips, and every line of that file reads as changed for everyone else.
#
# Declaring it here pins the policy to the repo, where a clone inherits it.

# Normalize every text file to LF in history; check out per the platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF even on Windows, or the shebang line carries a \r
# and the interpreter is "not found".
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows-only files that genuinely want CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary: never normalize, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
